WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.652
Tests convert expectations into executable evidence.

2
00:00:02.652 --> 00:00:08.397
A generated feature is not complete because the assistant says it is complete,

3
00:00:08.397 --> 00:00:12.817
and it is not complete merely because one demonstration works.

4
00:00:12.817 --> 00:00:16.353
A demo shows that one path succeeded once.

5
00:00:16.353 --> 00:00:22.982
Engineering validation asks what else could happen and how the software behaves when conditions change.

6
00:00:22.982 --> 00:00:26.076
The right validation depends on the change.

7
00:00:26.076 --> 00:00:29.612
Static analysis checks source code without running it.

8
00:00:29.612 --> 00:00:33.148
Formatting and linting catch style and common mistakes.

9
00:00:33.148 --> 00:00:36.242
Unit tests exercise small pieces of logic.

10
00:00:36.242 --> 00:00:39.335
Integration tests check how components work together.

11
00:00:39.335 --> 00:00:42.871
Type checking, build validation, manual behavior checks, logs,

12
00:00:42.871 --> 00:00:46.849
and runtime observations all reveal different kinds of evidence.

13
00:00:46.849 --> 00:00:49.059
A parser needs malformed-input tests.

14
00:00:49.059 --> 00:00:52.594
A user interface needs keyboard and accessibility checks.

15
00:00:52.594 --> 00:00:56.572
A database change may need migration and rollback testing.

16
00:00:56.572 --> 00:01:00.992
When something fails, give the assistant evidence rather than frustration.

17
00:01:00.992 --> 00:01:08.505
Useful debugging context includes the exact command that was run, the relevant error message, the expected behavior,

18
00:01:08.505 --> 00:01:12.925
the observed behavior, the smallest reproducible input, recent code changes,

19
00:01:12.925 --> 00:01:17.345
and environment details such as operating system or dependency versions.

20
00:01:17.345 --> 00:01:21.764
"It still does not work" leaves too many possibilities open.

21
00:01:21.764 --> 00:01:24.416
Reproduce the failure before changing code.

22
00:01:24.416 --> 00:01:33.256
If the problem cannot be repeated, you may be solving the wrong issue or treating a symptom as the cause.

23
00:01:33.256 --> 00:01:39.443
Once the failure is understood, create a regression test if the project allows it.

24
00:01:39.443 --> 00:01:45.189
A regression test fails for the original bug and passes after the fix,

25
00:01:45.189 --> 00:01:48.283
preserving the lesson learned for future changes.

26
00:01:48.283 --> 00:01:50.934
Evidence does not make judgment unnecessary.

27
00:01:50.934 --> 00:01:54.470
Tests can be incomplete, stale, or even wrong.

28
00:01:54.470 --> 00:02:01.100
Passing tests show that tested conditions passed; they do not prove every requirement, security property,

29
00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:03.310
or operating environment is correct.

30
00:02:03.310 --> 00:02:09.497
The disciplined workflow is to make expectations executable where practical, debug from observed facts,

31
00:02:09.497 --> 00:02:12.591
and expand the evidence when uncertainty remains.
